# Beast of Reincarnation (PPSA29343) -- advance the boot dialogs.
#
# The title's first interactive surface is its own "Digital Deluxe Version bonus received." dialog
# with a single OK button, reached at t~90 s. Without input it holds there for the rest of the run.
#
# Pulses, never a hold. Sonic Racing: CrossWorlds (#2358) is the closest analogue in the corpus --
# same engine generation, same publisher -- and there a HELD button advanced nothing: the guest
# needs a neutral->pressed transition. It cycles Cross, Circle, Options and Triangle so a screen
# bound to any of the four advances; Asterix Babylon's skip was Triangle and Tales of Graces f
# binds "go" to OPTIONS, so a Cross-only route has looped forever on four titles in this corpus.
#
# Frame anchors rather than seconds: this title publishes roughly 76 host frames/s early and
# roughly 35/s once the UI is up, so wall-clock anchors drift badly between runs while frame
# anchors do not.
#
# NOTE: reaching the dialog at all currently needs PROSPER_CB_EFC_NO_COLOR=1 (the #1588 A/B lever).
# On a default launch prosper's unmodeled ELIMINATE_FAST_CLEAR pass paints over the composite and
# every frame is a flat clear, so this route has nothing to act on. See
# prosper/docs/BEAST_OF_REINCARNATION_STATUS.md.
